  "fix": {
    "fix_type": "pipeline",
    "target_module": "fir_filter",
    "added_latency_cycles": 1,
    "modified_rtl": "module fir_filter #(parameter N=8, parameter WIDTH=16) (\n    input clk, input rst, input en,\n    input  signed [WIDTH-1:0] sample_in,\n    output signed [WIDTH-1:0] sample_out\n);\nreg signed [WIDTH-1:0] c [N-1:0];\nreg signed [WIDTH-1:0] Q [N-1:0];\nreg signed [40:0] imm;\nreg signed [40:0] psum_lo;\nreg signed [40:0] psum_hi;\ninteger i, j, k;\n\nalways @(posedge clk) begin\n    if (rst) begin\n        for (i=0; i<N; i=i+1) begin\n \n            Q[i] <= 0;\n        end\n        c[0] <= 16'sd3;  c[1] <= 16'sd11;  c[2] <= 16'sd24;  c[3] <= 16'sd31;\n        c[4] <= 16'sd31; c[5] <= 16'sd24;  c[6] <= 16'sd11;  c[7] <= 16'sd3;\n    end else if (en) begin        // <-- only shift on a genuine new sample\n        Q[0] <= sample_in;\n        for (j=1; j<N; j=j+1)\n            Q[j] <= Q[j-1];\n    end\n    // else: hold \u2014 no new sample this cycle, don't shift\nend\n\n// Pipeline stage 1: two 4-product half-sums registered to split the MAC chain\nalways @(posedge clk) begin\n    if (rst) begin\n        psum_lo <= 0;\n        psum_hi <= 0;\n    end else begin\n        psum_lo <= (c[0] * Q[0]) + (c[1] * Q[1]) + (c[2] * Q[2]) + (c[3] * Q[3]);\n        psum_hi <= (c[4] * Q[4]) + (c[5] * Q[5]) + (c[6] * Q[6]) + (c[7] * Q[7]);\n    end\nend\n\n// Pipeline stage 2: final reduction (combinational, as before)\nalways @(*) begin\n    imm = psum_lo + psum_hi;\nend\nassign sample_out = imm[WIDTH-1:0];\nendmodule",
    "rationale": "Strategy: PIPELINE. RETIME was rejected because the only registers touching this path are the Q[] tap-delay line and the constant c[] coefficients; Q[j] fans out both to its multiplier and to Q[j+1], so moving it across the multiplier would break the shift chain, and there is no register anywhere inside the multiply/adder array to reposition. So no legal existing-register move splits the chain.\n\nThe critical path is the unrolled MAC 'imm = imm + c[k]*Q[k]' in the always @(*) block: the XOR/XNOR band is partial-product generation for the 8 signed 16x16 products, the ~20 AOI21/OAI21 stages are the array/carry chain, and the trailing XNOR/XOR + OAI21/AND2/NOR3/MUX2 is the final CPA feeding the (out-of-scope) capture flop _6750_. This logic is in the shown RTL.\n\nCut location: the 8-term summation is broken into psum_lo = sum of products k=0..3 and psum_hi = sum of products k=4..7, both registered in a new posedge clk block (synchronous active-high reset, non-blocking, matching the existing style). The final psum_lo + psum_hi and the imm[WIDTH-1:0] truncation stay combinational. This halves the multiplier-array-plus-adder depth per stage.\n\nBalance: sample_out is the sole consumer of this logic. Both partial sums are delayed by exactly 1 cycle, so the reconverging final add is balanced. The Q[]/c[] shift/load behavior is unchanged. Result is bit-identical (two's-complement add is associative/commutative mod 2^41, the 41-bit accumulator cannot overflow for 8 products, and imm[15:0] truncation is independent of summation grouping); sample_out is simply produced one fir_clk cycle later. added_latency_cycles = 1."
